{"version":"1","id":"openshift","handle":"openshift","name":"OpenShift","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/7c1899f53da74d4490a7655e5a5566aa","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":1.6699,"y":-1.9934,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":309,"newest_post_at":"2023-11-17T14:00:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2021-04-22T17:38:24.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.009709,"listicle_ratio":0.003236,"question_ratio":0.019417,"avg_read_time":5.498382,"summary_length_avg":294.18123,"title_length_avg":64.799353,"title_length_var":548.775275,"tag_entropy":3.86775,"tag_diversity":0.466019,"top_tag_share":0.032362,"avg_upvotes":0.20712,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.003236,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.030769,"zero_engagement_share":0.81877,"viral_share":0.0,"posts_per_week":2.303911,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.430556},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[-7.5882,-6.7059],"cadence_depth":[6.3382,-0.9853],"hype_variety":[1.1912,6.4265],"title_style":[0.6618,0.3088]},"top_tags":[["openshift",213],["kubernetes",137],["red-hat",85],["cloud",58],["security",49],["infrastructure",48],["aws",34],["cloud-native",33]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["How to build a home Kubernetes lab with MicroShift and GitOps","Polling triggers in OpenShift Pipeline","Red Hat Congratulates Istio on graduating at the CNCF"],"outlier":["Object Detection with Red Hat OpenShift Data Science and Red Hat OpenShift Service on AWS Running on 3rd Generation Intel\u00ae Xeon\u00ae Scalable Processor Based Instances at AWS re:Invent"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"nXKEyhCOl","title":"What\u2019s new in Red Hat OpenShift Monitoring 4.14, Logging 5.8, and Distributed Tracing 2.9?","url":"https://content.cloud.redhat.com/blog/whats-new-in-red-hat-openshift-monitoring-4.14-logging-5.8-and-distributed-tracing-2.9","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-s-new-in-red-hat-openshift-monitoring-4-14-logging-5-8-and-distributed-tracing-2-9--nxkeyhcol","summary":"Red Hat OpenShift Observability introduces new features in Monitoring 4.14, Logging 5.8, and Distributed Tracing 2.9. It offers solutions to various problems, customizable alerting rules for admins, and enhancements in data storage.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f621a13810f2734776d45439d8f84145?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-17T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"Xfli8yBkO","title":"Announcing Red Hat OpenShift on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure with Virtual Machines","url":"https://content.cloud.redhat.com/blog/a-guide-to-red-hat-openshift-on-oracle-cloud-infrastructure-with-virtual-machines","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/announcing-red-hat-openshift-on-oracle-cloud-infrastructure-with-virtual-machines-xfli8ybko","summary":"Red Hat and Oracle announced the collaboration to bring Red Hat OpenShift to Oracle Cloud Infrastructure. The collaboration resulted in the availability of Red Hat OpenShift on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure with Virtual Machines (VMs) for Developer Preview. The deployment of OpenShift on Oracle Cloud Infrastructure with VMs is done through the Assisted Installer or the Agent-based Installer. Oracle provides integrations like Cloud Controller Manager (CCM) and Container Storage Interface (CSI) for this deployment.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f621a13810f2734776d45439d8f84145?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"eMAb5LJ8Z","title":"WebAssembly (WASM) and OpenShift: A Powerful Duo for Modern Applications","url":"https://content.cloud.redhat.com/blog/webassembly-wasm-and-openshift-a-powerful-duo-for-modern-applications","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/webassembly-wasm-and-openshift-a-powerful-duo-for-modern-applications-emab5lj8z","summary":"WebAssembly (WASM) and OpenShift can work together to create powerful, scalable, and efficient applications. WASM is a binary instruction format for a stack-based virtual machine, while OpenShift is a leading platform for deploying microservices, managing edge computing, and orchestrating serverless functions. The combination of WASM and OpenShift offers efficiency, cross-platform compatibility, and flexibility for developers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f621a13810f2734776d45439d8f84145?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"yRjocIKGD","title":"In-place Resource Resize of OpenShift Pod spec","url":"https://content.cloud.redhat.com/blog/in-place-resource-resize-of-openshift-pod-spec","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/in-place-resource-resize-of-openshift-pod-spec-yrjocikgd","summary":"In-place resource resizing allows for adjusting the CPU and memory resources of a running Pod without recreating it, reducing downtime and improving resource utilization. It is important for efficient resource management and cost savings. This feature is available in Red Hat OpenShift.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f621a13810f2734776d45439d8f84145?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-14T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"ueZwV7muA","title":"Introducing the Secret Store CSI Driver in OpenShift","url":"https://content.cloud.redhat.com/blog/introducing-the-secret-store-csi-driver-in-openshift","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/introducing-the-secret-store-csi-driver-in-openshift-uezwv7mua","summary":"Learn about the importance of securing Kubernetes secrets and how the Secret Store CSI Driver works in OpenShift.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f621a13810f2734776d45439d8f84145?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-13T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"QoCukZ5yN","title":"Accelerate Cluster Upgrades with TALM's Workload Image Pre-Caching","url":"https://content.cloud.redhat.com/blog/accelerate-cluster-upgrades-with-talms-workload-image-pre-caching","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/accelerate-cluster-upgrades-with-talm-s-workload-image-pre-caching-qocukz5yn","summary":"This blog post explores how TALM's workload image pre-caching feature helps in accelerating cluster upgrades by reducing downtime and optimizing bandwidth utilization. It explains the process of configuring pre-caching using the PreCachingConfig CRD and provides verification steps to ensure successful pre-caching of workload images.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f621a13810f2734776d45439d8f84145?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-10T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"V8gPd7ZUk","title":"Introducing Selectable Profiles for etcd","url":"https://content.cloud.redhat.com/blog/introducing-selectable-profiles-for-etcd","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/introducing-selectable-profiles-for-etcd-v8gpd7zuk","summary":"The article discusses the introduction of selectable profiles for etcd in OpenShift 4.14, which allows cluster administrators to change the etcd profile to better match their environment. The article also provides information about the default and slow profiles of the OpenShift etcd Operator and gives instructions on how to change the etcd profile.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f621a13810f2734776d45439d8f84145?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-10T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"0Tvmyzie0","title":"Faster Onboarding for New Infrastructure Providers with Red Hat OpenShift\u2019s External Platform","url":"https://content.cloud.redhat.com/blog/faster-onboarding-for-new-infrastructure-providers-with-red-hat-openshifts-external-platform","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/faster-onboarding-for-new-infrastructure-providers-with-red-hat-openshift-s-external-platform-0tvmyzie0","summary":"Red Hat OpenShift introduces the external platform, which allows partners to customize infrastructure components for easier integration. It enables the installation of cloud provider components and facilitates the utilization of cloud storage drivers and controllers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f621a13810f2734776d45439d8f84145?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"pIjPZgFl6","title":"Your Guide to vSphere CSI Migration","url":"https://content.cloud.redhat.com/blog/your-guide-to-vsphere-csi-migration","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/your-guide-to-vsphere-csi-migration-pijpzgfl6","summary":"CSI migration allows storage drivers to be independent of the Kubernetes release cycle. OpenShift supports CSI migration for various drivers, including vSphere. Upgrades may be blocked for clusters using in-tree PVs, but can be unlocked by updating vSphere or providing administrator acknowledgement. It is safe to enable CSI migration in OCP 4.13 if running on vSphere 7.0u3L+ or 8.0u2+.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f621a13810f2734776d45439d8f84145?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-11-09T14:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"P18lLHbLL","title":"Extending Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform to AWS Local Zones","url":"https://content.cloud.redhat.com/blog/extending-red-hat-openshift-container-platform-to-aws-local-zones","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/extending-red-hat-openshift-container-platform-to-aws-local-zones-p18llhbll","summary":"OpenShift Container Platform can be extended to AWS Local Zones, providing benefits such as improved application performance and user experience, cost savings, and compliance with data residency requirements.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/f621a13810f2734776d45439d8f84145?_a=AQAEufR","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at"